Netnews distribution can at times be a little unpredictable; for example,
if Fyodor Antonov posts something from some random machine in Russia, and
then Alan Bloggs posts a follow-up from some random machine in the UK,
Heidi Sanchez's news server in Berkeley, California, USA might receive
Alan's article before it receives Fyodor's.  It might even receive the
follow-up Johann Schmidt in Germany posted to Alan's article before it
receives Alan's follow-up to Fyodor's article.

(This is much less likely these days in Big 8 groups, of course.)
